			"type":"text",
			"text":"#### Reflections",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1435,
			"y":160,
			"width":330,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"daaa9b9cf4d607bf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"```base\nfilters:\n  and:\n    - 'file.inFolder(\"ThePlan/System/_reflections\")'\nviews:\n  - type: list\n    name: Reflections\n    order:\n      - file.name\n    sort:\n      - property: file.mtime\n        direction: DESC\n\n```\n",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":null
			},
			"x":-1480,
			"y":240,
			"width":420,
			"height":540
		},
		{
			"id":"05c3158ada68d593",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Journaling",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":1240,
			"y":-60,
			"width":360,
			"height":80
		},
		{"id":"f16dc78f043514e4","type":"file","file":"System/Plans.md","x":165,"y":123,"width":720,"height":920},
		{
			"id":"b70b3c5b10c9dd40",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Weekly/Monthly\n- ### Why?\n\t- To check if any insights were missed\n\t- By re-reading week's dreams I may find some pattern. Since the unconscious has lots of inertia - it operates on big scales as well. Like yeah, it can give insight for the next day, but also at the same time that insight might have additional message for like a next week or a next month. So this ritual of re-reading can help with that too.\n\t- less about writing some big journal entry, and more about just reviewing the last X days or X weeks. To get that \"continuity/progression of my life\" feeling. May be helpful.\n\t- Insight of dreams may be forgotten\n\t- \nWeekly stuff for summarizing progress in a few sentences so one can track progress solely on weekly summarizations. And on top of that - to extract insights and so on...\n\nDaily log, based on publish. Either as journal entry OR on main page of the site",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":1080,
			"y":123,
			"width":680,
			"height":797
		},
		{
			"id":"4470d580d7667ab7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Schedule\nWhy? \nTo see negative impact of temptations\nTo see tasks to do beforehand, which allows to unconsciously prepare and easier to start\nComplex possession kills time and memory, if your honest in schedule - it fixes that issue",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":null
			},
			"x":1320,
			"y":-560,
			"width":460,
			"height":280
		},
		{"id":"3f89ff006c0cd466","type":"file","file":"Obsidian.md","x":237,"y":-980,"width":935,"height":700}
	],
